    "posts": [
      {
        "id": 6189,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-08-22T23:40:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hey, folks. Didn't know if everyone else already knew this, but I just figured it out and wanted to share.  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=9\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\"></p>\n<p>At Gen Con, some folks commented about typos and other errors in both the Enhanced Edition and Infernal Relics rulebooks. It turns out that <a href=\"http://sentinelsofthemultiverse.com/downloads\">the online versions</a> are actually updated with the corrections!  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/open_mouth.png?v=9\" title=\":open_mouth:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":open_mouth:\">  That’s shiny!</p>\n<p>I've printed out versions for my travel box, so I have extras without the errors (although I'll admit we rarely refer to the rulebook except when teaching new folks how to play  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/blush.png?v=9\" title=\":blush:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":blush:\"> ).</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:36:03.504Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
        "reads": 1,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 5.2,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 6187,
        "topic_slug": "the-rulebooks-in-downloads-are-the-latest-and-greatest",
        "display_username": "Rabit",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
        "flair_bg_color": "",
        "flair_color": "",
